course: dictionary
lesson: 6497
title: Nebula: a cloud in space
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A nebula is a huge cloud of gas and dust in space. You can work out its meaning from the clues around it. «About 4.6 billion years ago there was no Sun and no Earth, only a huge, cold cloud of gas and dust called the solar nebula.» The words "cloud of gas and dust" tell you what a nebula is, and "called the solar nebula" shows that the nebula is a kind of cloud.
explain: Use the swap check. Put "huge cloud of gas and dust" in place of "nebula" in the sentence: «The Sun formed long ago from a huge cloud of gas and dust.» It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: Be careful with «planetary nebula». It has nothing to do with planets. It got its name because it looked like a round planet in old telescopes. The clue is in the word "planetary", but the sentence tells you the truth behind it.
fact: A nebula is a huge cloud of gas and dust in space.
fact: Some nebulae are places where new stars are being born.
fact: Other nebulae are what is left after a star dies.
fact: The plural of «nebula» can be «nebulae» or «nebulas».
fact: The Sun formed from a nebula long ago, about 4.6 billion years ago.
exercise: «The Solar System formed from a huge cloud of gas and dust called the solar nebula.» What is a nebula? | *A huge cloud of gas and dust in space | A bright star that never dies | A kind of telescope | A small rocky planet
exercise: Which word is a plural of nebula? | nebulon | nebules | *nebulae | nebuli
exercise: «A planetary nebula has nothing to do with planets.» Why did it get that name? | *It looked like a round planet in old telescopes | It is the closest planet to the Sun | It was discovered on a planet | It is a planet made of gas
test: Some nebulae are places where what happens? | *New stars are being born | Telescopes are built | Planets are made of ice | Old trees grow
test: Hubble and James Webb take colourful photos of what? | Oceans | *Nebulae | Schools | Forests
exam: The Crab Nebula is what is left after what? | *An exploding star | A planet is born | A comet melts | A river dries up
